temper (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * First release as temper, renamed from tempered (history at
    https://github.com/charlieh0tel/tempered-hid).  Two packages:
    temper, the command-line tool (temper read, info, log), and
    temper-iio, the daemon that presents a TEMPerGold or TEMPerHUM as
    Linux IIO devices.
  * The daemon's unit, user, settings and links are named temper-iio:
    temper-iio@, /etc/default/temper-iio with TEMPER_IIO_* settings,
    /run/temper-iio.
  * On crates.io: temper-hid, the library (was tempered-hid; API
    hid::Device, Stick::reading, Celsius, RelativeHumidityPercent,
    schedule::Schedule), and temper-hid-cli, the temper tool.
  * Linux only for now; Windows support is planned.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 23:12:45 -0700
